Reconstruct A and B propositions from shared and side-specific fragments before
claiming a loss. For each decisive delta name its actual meaning, its counterpart
or absence, and its function: covered UI, same-record addition, independent record,
or identity/state/permission boundary. Then assign the three consistent scores.

An Accept button does not erase B's written continued-browsing consent condition.
A Stories/byline pointer alone does not prove an unseen article. Added FAQ actions
are retained; headings whose meaning is in the shared answers can be covered.
New access restrictions are permission changes even in a long substantive policy;
absence of a contradictory sentence does not make them ordinary extensions.
Preserve actual differing recipients, SKUs, directory paths, dates and list members.
Give each active field its OWN real bilateral anchor and decisive delta citations.

<semantic_diff status="{{ payload.semantic_diff_evidence.status }}"
 contract="{{ payload.semantic_diff_evidence.contract_version }}">
counts: {{ payload.semantic_diff_evidence.span_counts }}
{% for span in payload.semantic_diff_evidence.spans %}
{% if span.kind == "SHARED" %}
[{{ span.span_id }} SHARED]
A: {{ span.a_text }}
B: {{ span.b_text }}
{% else %}
[{{ span.span_id }} {{ span.kind }}] {{ span.text }}
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
</semantic_diff>

{% if repair_feedback %}
<repair_retry>
The previous result failed local validation. Return a fresh judgment addressing
this safe structured issue: {{ repair_feedback }}
</repair_retry>
{% endif %}
